    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/33683": {
      "title": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Open Rank Non Tenure Track Positions, Kelley School of Business (International Business)",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Open Rank Non Tenure Track Positions, Kelley School of Business (International Business) Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Open Rank Non Tenure Track Positions, Kelley School of Business (International Business) Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Interested candidates should review the application requirements and submit their application at https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/33677 . Applications must be received by October 5, 2026 to be assured of full consideration; however, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Posting Details Position Details Title Open Rank Non Tenure Track Positions, Kelley School of Business (International Business) Appointment Status Non-Tenure Track Department IU Bloomington Management and Entrepreneurship Location Bloomington Position Summary The Management & Entrepreneurship (M&E) department at the Kelley School of Business, Indiana University-Bloomington invites applicants for an open rank non-tenure-track faculty position in the International Business area to begin fall 2027. Basic Qualifications For a candidate to be considered at the Clinical classification, a Ph.D. or DBA degree in management or a related field is required and must be completed by no later than August 2027. Candidates to be considered at the Lecturer classification must have a master’s degree in the area of appointment (international business, management or related field. We encourage applications from candidates who have significant professional experience and, ideally, experience teaching at the undergraduate and graduate levels; teaching experience in the online modality is also highly desirable. Department Contact for Questions Questions regarding the positions or application process can be directed to Ms. Jennifer Wyrick (mgmtrecr@iu.edu). Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Special Instructions Interested candidates should review the application requirements and submit their application at https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/33677 . Applications must be received by October 5, 2026 to be assured of full consideration; however, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. For Best Consideration Date 10/05/2026 Expected Start Date 08/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101595-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Evidence of Teaching Ability Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Sample Syllabus Course Evaluation Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
